---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Patio Privacy Planner" description="Create a patio privacy worksheet with a scaled boundary sketch, example screen counts, optional cost arithmetic, and a practical checklist."><header class="container page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Free planning tool · No account needed</p><h1>Patio Privacy Planner</h1><p class="lead">Choose a starting approach for more privacy, map an example screen layout, and save a checklist before you buy.</p></header><section class="container section planner-layout"><form class="panel planner-form" id="privacy-form"><fieldset><legend><span>1</span> Measure your space</legend><label for="space">Outdoor space</label><select id="space"><option value="patio">Ground-level patio</option><option value="balcony">Balcony</option></select><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="patio-width">Outdoor width (ft)</label><input id="patio-width" type="number" min="1" max="100" step="0.5" value="10" required/></div><div><label for="depth">Outdoor depth (ft)</label><input id="depth" type="number" min="2" max="100" step="0.5" value="8" required/></div></div><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="width">Width to screen (ft)</label><input id="width" type="number" min="1" max="100" step="0.5" value="6" required/></div><div><label for="screen-height">Target height (ft)</label><input id="screen-height" type="number" min="1" max="10" step="0.5" value="6" required/></div></div><p class="small">Plan one straight boundary. Height is a preference to research, not a safe-height recommendation. Measure from the seating position you want to protect.</p></fieldset><fieldset><legend><span>2</span> Choose your priorities</legend><label for="need">Main priority</label><select id="need"><option value="view">Block a direct sightline</option><option value="flex">Easy to move or store</option><option value="green">Add greenery</option></select><label for="budget">Planning budget</label><select id="budget"><option value="low">Under $100 — try existing items first</option><option value="medium" selected>$100–$300 — compare a focused solution</option><option value="high">Over $300 — compare complete systems</option></select><p class="small">Budget bands guide the planning approach; they do not assume current product prices.</p><label for="exposure">Wind exposure</label><select id="exposure"><option value="exposed" selected>Exposed or unsure</option><option value="sheltered">Sheltered; product limits still apply</option></select><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" id="approved"/> For a balcony, I have confirmed permission, permitted loads, drainage, and wind restrictions with building management.</label></fieldset><fieldset><legend><span>3</span> Compare an example layout</legend><label for="panel-width">Usable width per example module (ft)</label><input id="panel-width" type="number" min="1" max="10" step="0.5" value="3" required/><p class="small">Use an actual product's usable width if known. The default is a paper-layout assumption, not a product recommendation. Supports and overlaps may change fit.</p><details class="cost-details"><summary>Optional: estimate using your own prices</summary><label for="module-price">Price per module (USD)</label><input id="module-price" type="number" min="0" max="100000" step="0.01" placeholder="Leave blank if unknown"/><label for="extra-cost">Additional costs (USD)</label><input id="extra-cost" type="number" min="0" max="100000" step="0.01" value="0"/><p class="small">Include supports, delivery, or taxes in additional costs. No prices are retrieved from retailers.</p></details></fieldset><div class="plan-actions"><button class="button" type="submit">Create my plan →</button><button class="reset-button" type="reset">Start over</button></div><p class="small">Your answers stay in this page. Nothing is sent to us or stored automatically.</p><noscript><p>JavaScript is needed for the interactive worksheet. Read our <a href="/articles/patio-privacy-ideas-for-renters/">patio privacy guide</a> for the planning steps.</p></noscript></form><section class="panel planner-result" aria-label="Your patio privacy worksheet"><h2>Your privacy plan</h2><div id="results" role="region" aria-label="Planner results" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" tabindex="-1"><div class="planner-empty"><img src="/assets/patio-layout.svg" alt="Example patio diagram with targeted screening and an open path." width="960" height="640"/><h3>A little planning before shopping.</h3><p>Enter your dimensions and preferences to get a starting approach, an example layout, and a checklist you can save or print.</p><p class="small">Exposed sites and unapproved balconies get a restrictions-first plan. The sketch never approves structural loads or installations.</p></div></div></section></section><section class="container planner-guidance"><h2>What this tool does</h2><p>It compares starting approaches and calculates straight-line example coverage. It does not select or test products, determine required supports, assess wind or loads, check building codes, or guarantee privacy at a particular height.</p><p>Read the <a href="/articles/patio-privacy-ideas-for-renters/">patio privacy guide</a> or <a href="/articles/small-patio-furniture-layout/">small patio layout guide</a> before making changes.</p></section><script type="module" src="/assets/planner.js" is:inline></script></Base>
